\DOC ENSURES_EXISTING_PRESERVED_TAC

\TYPE {ENSURES_EXISTING_PRESERVED_TAC : term -> tactic}

\SYNOPSIS
Given a state component {ctm}, transforms an {ensures} goal whose precondition
fixes the value of {ctm} by appending that same equation to the postcondition
and adding {ctm} to the frame of changeable components.

\DESCRIBE
The argument {ctm : term} is the state component whose precondition-fixed value
is to be asserted in the postcondition and added to the frame. The goal must be
of the form {ensures m P Q F} where {P} contains a conjunct equating the read
of {ctm} to some term; that equation is appended as a final conjunct of {Q},
and {MAYCHANGE [ctm]} is joined to the frame. The resulting precondition {P'}
states the same conditions as {P} but with its conjunction re-associated into a
flat right-nested form, so nested bracketed groups of conjuncts are flattened.
{
   A ?- ensures m P Q F
   ========================================================  ENSURES_EXISTING_PRESERVED_TAC ctm
   A ?- ensures m P' Q' (F ,, MAYCHANGE [ctm])
}

\COMMENTS
The observed traces show only this single kind of transformation, always on
{ensures} goals for the same machine model whose precondition already
constrains the given component.

\ENDDOC
